================================================================================
PRE-LOAD GATE - harness/bin/run-joern.sh (Stage 3, the third of four heap-bound JVMs)
harness/artifacts/logs/joern.preflight.log
================================================================================

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS

  AAP 0.6.4 and 0.8.2 require the graph identity recorded at write time to be
  RECOMPUTED AND COMPARED immediately before EVERY load, with each check logged,
  and a mismatch halts. This is that check for the Stage 3 Joern runner load. It
  also records, before the load rather than after it, the three other conditions
  that decide whether the load is even permitted: the JDK major must be 21, the
  host must be shown to COMMIT the heap rather than merely reserve it, and the
  smoke override must be unset. Verification is independent of the thing verified:
  every value below is measured here, not copied from a record that states it.

  The runner prints its own graph identity lines (cpg / cpg bytes / cpg sha256)
  into its console stream, which is the in-stream half of this same evidence and
  is preserved verbatim in harness/artifacts/logs/joern.stdout.log.

ENVIRONMENT
  Sourced in a fresh non-login shell: env -i BLITZY_CLONE_INDEX=31 bash --noprofile --norc, then . harness/env.sh
  Clone index    : 31 (this clone). HARNESS_SCRATCH_DIR is derived from it, and two
                   Joern processes sharing one workspace corrupt each other.
  Generated at   : 2026-08-24T22:38:19+00:00

