================================================================================
POST-CHECK - A SIDE EFFECT OF THE VERSION READ ABOVE, OBSERVED AND CLEARED
================================================================================

  Joern has no --workspace flag and writes a ./workspace directory into whatever
  directory it is started from. The banner read in PART 3 ran with this
  repository as its working directory, so it created ./workspace in the
  repository root at 2026-08-24T22:38:54Z. It was EMPTY - it held no project,
  because reading the banner with stdin closed loads nothing - and it was removed
  with rmdir, which can only succeed on an empty directory:

$ find workspace -mindepth 1 | wc -l
[stdout]
0
[exit] 0

$ rmdir workspace
[stdout]
[exit] 0

$ ls -d workspace
[stderr]
ls: cannot access 'workspace': No such file or directory
[exit] 2

  This is recorded rather than quietly cleaned because the same mechanism is why
  harness/bin/run-joern.sh cds to $HARNESS_SCRATCH_DIR/joern-run before invoking
  joern: the scan itself writes its ~2.9 GB workspace there, per clone, and never
  into the repository. That behaviour is unaffected by the line above, and the
  repository holds no workspace directory after this gate.
